{{!-- The Tags Directory: a Surface that lists subjects, not posts.

Its sibling Surface, the tag archive at /tag/{slug}/, lists one tag's posts — see tag.hbs. They
look alike in the card layout and they are not the same thing; CONTEXT.md was written to settle
exactly this.

Shared by page-tags.hbs and custom-tags.hbs so no markup is duplicated: the first keeps the demo
slug working, the second lets a buyer apply this layout to a page named anything at all.

ORDERED BY NAME. A directory is browsed, and a browsed list is alphabetical — which is also the
order the design draws. `limit="100"` is declared rather than `"all"` because Ghost 6 caps every
{{#get}} at 100 silently (core/shared/max-limit-cap.js); a publication past that many public tags
loses the end of the alphabet, and ghost/README.md says so rather than the theme reordering the
Surface to hide it.

`{{#if tags}}` and not the get's `{{else}}`: get calls `options.inverse` only for an invalid
resource or an API error (core/frontend/helpers/get.js), never for an empty result. --}}
{{#post}}
	{{> "page-intro" eyebrow=(t "Browse") headingId="tags-title"}}

	{{#get "tags" include="count.posts" order="name asc" limit="100" as |tags|}}
		{{#if tags}}
			{{#match @custom.directory_layout "Cover cards"}}
				{{> "directory/tag-cards" tags=tags}}
			{{else}}
				{{> "directory/tag-rows" tags=tags}}
			{{/match}}
		{{else}}
			<section class="container pt-16">
				<p class="font-body text-muted">{{t "No tags yet."}}</p>
			</section>
		{{/if}}
	{{/get}}

	{{> "newsletter" anchor="tags-newsletter" pt="pt-20"}}
{{/post}}
